# Phase 5: OpenSearch

Index articles.

Document:

```json
{
  "title": "AI News",
  "content": "...",
  "sentiment": "positive"
}
```

Now users can search.

```text
User
  ↓
Streamlit
  ↓
FastAPI
  ↓
OpenSearch
```

---

# Phase 6: Semantic Search

You're already familiar with embeddings from your Snowflake/OpenSearch work.

Add:

```python
sentence-transformers
```

Generate embeddings:

```python
embedding = model.encode(article)
```

Store in OpenSearch.

Now users can search:

```text
"positive AI startup news"
```

instead of exact keywords.

---

# Phase 7: Docker Compose

Today you probably have:

```text
docker run sentiment-app
```

Upgrade to:

```yaml
services:
  streamlit:
  fastapi:
  postgres:
  opensearch:
```

One command:

```bash
docker compose up
```

This is a major step toward platform engineering.

---

# Phase 8: GitHub Actions

Since your code is already in GitHub, add CI.

Pipeline:

```text
GitHub Push
     ↓
Run Tests
     ↓
Build Docker Image
     ↓
Publish Artifact
```

You don't need AWS yet.

Learn:

* CI/CD
* Automated testing
* Container builds

---

# Phase 9: Observability

Add:

* Prometheus
* Grafana

Track:

```text
